# BUG FIX (reported CI failure on all three OSes): this used to be just
# `build/` — an exact-name match that does NOT cover `build-cli-sidecar/`,
# `build-cli/`, `build-verify/`, `build-asan/`, or any other local CMake
# scratch directory a developer (or this engineering session) creates
# alongside it. `build-cli-sidecar/` specifically had its CMakeCache.txt
# committed as a result — a file that bakes in the exact local absolute
# path it was configured from — which then made every fresh CI checkout
# (Windows, Linux, AND macOS runners all showed the same committer's local
# Windows path in their error output) fail with "CMakeCache.txt directory
# ... is different than the directory ... where it was created", since
# CMake correctly refuses to reuse a cache recorded against a path that
# isn't the current one. `build*/` (trailing slash: directories only, so
# it can't accidentally also match the `build-and-run.sh`/`.ps1` FILES at
# the repo root) covers this whole family of directories generically
# instead of needing a new .gitignore line every time a new one shows up.
# (build.rs also got a matching defensive fix: it now detects and wipes a
# stale/mismatched cache itself rather than hard-failing, so this class of
# problem can't come back even if a build dir slips past this ignore rule
# some other way — e.g. `git add -f`.)
build*/
*.o
*.a
web/node_modules
web/dist
.DS_Store

# Tauri app — Cargo.lock IS committed (this is an application, not a library;
# Rust convention keeps the lockfile for binaries/apps for reproducible builds).
tauri-app/node_modules
tauri-app/dist
tauri-app/src-tauri/target
tauri-app/src-tauri/gen
# CLI sidecar binaries (Tauri externalBin — tauri.conf.json's bundle.
# externalBin) are built fresh by CI immediately before each `tauri build`
# (see .github/workflows/tauri-release.yml's "Build CLI sidecar" step) and
# are OS/arch-specific — never something to commit. The directory itself
# (with its README) stays tracked so `bundle.externalBin`'s referenced path
# exists in a fresh checkout even before that step has ever run.
tauri-app/src-tauri/binaries/*
!tauri-app/src-tauri/binaries/README.md


# Env files
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production
.env.*


